message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "A Constructible Tower Approaching Pi: Explicit Compass-and-Straightedge Approximants under Transparent Algebraic Acceleration"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Baker
    given-names: C. Wayne
date-released: 2026-11-10
version: v1.3
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24109048
repository-code: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/constructible-tower-approaching-pi"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24109048"
abstract: >-
  An explicit compass-and-straightedge constructible polygonal tower,
  accelerated by a rational Richardson-Romberg recurrence, approaches the
  nonconstructible limit pi. The revised analysis derives the diagonal error
  and the corrected quadratic digit-growth coefficient log10(2).
keywords:
  - constructible numbers
  - compass and straightedge
  - pi
  - polygonal approximation
  - Richardson extrapolation
  - Romberg extrapolation
  - geometric approximation
